---
title: "Pilot Study: Difficulty and Interest Ratings"
author: "Przemysław Marcowski, PhD"
---



## Overview

The pilot study compared how the same tasks were rated in experimental and survey contexts. Bayesian paired-sample tests quantify context differences in perceived difficulty and interest.

## Design and sample

Each participant rated task difficulty and interest in both contexts. The prepared dataset contains one row per participant; no participant-level records are displayed.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Read pilot data
pilot_data <- readRDS("../data/prepared/pilot.Rds")
```
:::



::: {.cell tbl-cap='Pilot sample'}

```{.r .cell-code}
tibble(
  Metric = c("Participants", "Mean age", "Age SD"),
  Value = c(
    n_distinct(pilot_data$id),
    mean(pilot_data$age, na.rm = TRUE),
    sd(pilot_data$age, na.rm = TRUE)
  )
) %>%
  gt::gt() %>%
  gt::fmt_number(columns = Value, decimals = 1)
```

