## Interpretation

Positive effects indicate higher ratings in the experimental context; negative effects indicate higher ratings in the survey context. The posterior means and 99% HDIs describe the magnitude and uncertainty of each difference, while the Bayes factors compare the paired-difference model with the null.

## Supplement and reproducibility

The tests use a Cauchy prior with scale 0.707, 10,000 posterior draws per comparison, a 99% interval, and a fixed random seed.


